    <div class="md:p-6 p-3 container">
      <h2>Questions and Answers</h2>
      <FAQ question="What is this?">
    Warthog is implementing a completely new DeFi model supporting a matching engine, which, in a one-of-a-kind way combines <em>two</em> sources of liquidity in a fair and MEV-proof way: 
    <ul>
      <li>discrete liquidity in the form of order books</li>
      <li>continuous liquidity in the form of a liquidity pool</li>
    </ul>
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question='What do you mean by "MEV-proof"?'>
        Sandwich attacks are one of the most dreaded DeFi attacks. They are part of a bigger problem called <em>front-running</em> which is inherently caused by that fact that in current DeFi designs reordering of transactions has an effect on their fill price. This is highly unfair against traders because their transactions are regularly sandwiched (front-run and back-run) by exploiters of this design. For example they buy before normal buy orders are executed, and sell immediately afterwards, essentially doing arbitrage trading within a block and causing financial loss to their victims. Reordering of Warthog's transactions won't have any effect such that sandwich attacks are not possible.
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question="What is a matching engine?">
          Simply put, in TradFi (Traditional Finance) a <em>matching engine</em> is a program or routine that matches buy and sell orders. It is responsible for deciding which orders are matched and deducting fees. In Warthog we do not only match buy and sell orders, but also pool liquidity.
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question='What are "WART" and "TOKEN"?'>
          WART is the native currency in Warthog. In this demo it acts as the quote currency. TOKEN acts as a generic placeholder for any Warthog tradable token (a feature that we are working on) that takes the role of the base currency.
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question="What are base and quote currencies?">
        In finance terms, when talking about trading a currency pair, the currency that you are trading, i.e. buying or selling, is called <em>base currency</em>, whereas the other, the one with respect to which you are expressing the price, is called <em>quote currency</em>. In this example TOKEN is the base currency since we are refering buy/sell terms to TOKEN, and WART is the quote currency since we are expressing the prices in WART.
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question="What are the gray, black and yellow colors expressing?">
        For easier visualization we use the following color-codes:
        <ul>
          <li>Gray: TOKEN amount</li>
          <li>Black: WART amount</li>
          <li>Yellow: Price</li>
        </ul>
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question="What is the pool fee?">
        It is the share that the liquidity pool keeps from a swap that goes through the pool instead of matching another order directly.
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question="Why is the buy order amount measured in WART but not in TOKEN despite I am buying TOKEN?">
        In DeFi trades are specified as swaps, i.e. the input amount is specified for both trade directions 
        <ul>
          <li>When you swap from WART to TOKEN the WART to be swapped is specified.</li>
          <li>When you swap from TOKEN to WART the WART to be swapped is specified.</li>
        </ul>
        If we create an order book with TOKEN base currency out of these swaps, the buy orders are swaps that specify the WART amount to be swapped into TOKEN in contrast to traditional order books which would instead specify the TOKEN amount to buy with WART.
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question="How does matching work in Warthog?">
        The matching mechanism that we invented at Warthog works by finding a price <em>p</em> at which the situation between buy and sell orders is saturated, i.e.
        <ol>
          <li>Buys are saturated: Either all swaps from WART to TOKEN at current limit price or above are filled, or additional swaps would move the price down below a limit swap that was partially matched already.</li>
          <li>Sells are saturated: Either all swaps from TOKEN to WART at current limit price or below are filled, or additional swaps would move the price up above a limit swap that was partially matched already.</li>
          <li>Some buy or sell pressure goes to the pool to move the price to <em>p</em></li>
        </ol>
        There exists only one such price and our algorithm determines this price.
      </FAQ>
      <FAQ question="I placed both a buy and a sell order at the same price, but only one side filled. Why?">
        The other side was satisfied by the liquidity pool instead. When the
        pool price isn't exactly at your order's price, one side can swap
        directly with the pool more cheaply than matching your order. This is
        the Fair Batch Matching equilibrium, not a bug. To force a direct match,
        set a limit price that crosses the pool price enough to make the other
        side prefer your order.
      </FAQ>
    <script>
      import FbmEngine from "warthog-fbm";
      import LeaderLine from "leader-line-new";

      const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

      // ── Shareable URL state ─────────────────────────────────────────
      // The engine is the source of truth, so the link is generated from
      // it rather than from a parallel JS model. Limits travel as their
      // raw price-grid bits (limitBits), so a restored book is identical
      // to the shared one. The decimal limit string is only a rendering,
      // recomputed from the bits, and is never stored in the link.
      const STATE_PARAM = "state";

      function encodeState() {
        return encodeMatch(state.lastMatch, engine.getConfig());
      }

      function encodeMatch(m, cfg) {
        if (!m) return "";
        // [limitBits, amount]: the exact price-grid value and the swap
        // amount. The decimal limit is not stored, it is derived from
        // the bits plus baseDecimals for display.
        const orders = (rows) => rows.map((o) => [o.limitBits, o.amount]);
        const payload = {
          v: 1,
          bd: cfg.baseDecimals,
          fee: cfg.feeE4,
          pool: [m.poolBefore.base, m.poolBefore.quote],
          buys: orders(m.buys),
          sells: orders(m.sells),
        };
        const bytes = new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(payload));
        let bin = "";
        for (const b of bytes) bin += String.fromCharCode(b);
        return btoa(bin).replace(/\+/g, "-").replace(/\//g, "_").replace(/=+$/, "");
      }

      function decodeState(raw) {
        const b64 = raw.replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/");
        const bin = atob(b64 + "=".repeat((4 - (b64.length % 4)) % 4));
        const json = new TextDecoder().decode(
          Uint8Array.from(bin, (c) => c.charCodeAt(0)),
        );
        const p = JSON.parse(json);
        if (!p || p.v !== 1) throw new Error("unsupported state version");
        if (!Number.isInteger(p.bd) || p.bd < 0 || p.bd > 18)
          throw new Error("invalid baseDecimals");
        if (!Number.isInteger(p.fee) || p.fee < 0 || p.fee > 9999)
          throw new Error("invalid feeE4");
        if (!Array.isArray(p.pool) || p.pool.length !== 2)
          throw new Error("invalid pool");
        const isOrder = (o) =>
          Array.isArray(o) &&
          o.length === 2 &&
          Number.isInteger(o[0]) &&
          typeof o[1] === "string";
        for (const o of p.buys ?? []) if (!isOrder(o)) throw new Error("invalid buy");
        for (const o of p.sells ?? []) if (!isOrder(o)) throw new Error("invalid sell");
        return p;
      }

      function readStateFromUrl() {
        const raw = new URL(window.location.href).searchParams.get(STATE_PARAM);
        if (!raw) return null;
        try {
          return decodeState(raw);
        } catch (err) {
          // A malformed link must not break the demo: fall back to the
          // default state and say so in the console.
          console.warn("Ignoring malformed ?state parameter:", err);
          return null;
        }
      }

      // Writes the current state into the address bar. replaceState (not
      // pushState) keeps the browser history clean while the user types
      // in the pool fields, and the write is debounced because browsers
      // rate-limit history updates.
      //
      // The untouched default demo keeps a clean URL: the parameter is
      // only added once the demo differs from the default state.
      let urlSyncTimer = null;
      let defaultState = null;
      function scheduleUrlSync() {
        if (urlSyncTimer) clearTimeout(urlSyncTimer);
        urlSyncTimer = setTimeout(() => {
          urlSyncTimer = null;
          try {
            const url = new URL(window.location.href);
            const encoded = encodeState();
            if (encoded && encoded !== defaultState) url.searchParams.set(STATE_PARAM, encoded);
            else url.searchParams.delete(STATE_PARAM);
            history.replaceState(null, "", url.toString());
          } catch (err) {
            console.warn("Could not update the URL:", err);
          }
        }, 150);
      }

      // Engine is permissive; we own field validity on the JS side and
      // gate engine.match() on it.
      let engine = null;
      let restored = null;
      try {
        await FbmEngine.init();
        restored = readStateFromUrl();
        engine = new FbmEngine(
          restored
            ? { baseDecimals: restored.bd, feeE4: restored.fee }
            : { baseDecimals: 8, feeE4: 5 },
        );
      } catch (err) {
        document.body.innerHTML = `<pre>Failed to load FBM engine: ${err.message}</pre>`;
        throw err;
      }

      // ── State model ────────────────────────────────────────────────
      const state = {
        poolBase:   { valid: true,  error: "" },  // HTML defaults 100, 200
        poolQuote:  { valid: true,  error: "" },
        fee:        { valid: true,  error: "" },  // HTML default 0.05%
        buyLimit:   { valid: false, error: "" },
        buyAmount:  { valid: false, error: "" },
        sellLimit:  { valid: false, error: "" },
        sellAmount: { valid: false, error: "" },
        lastMatch: null,
      };

      // ── DOM refs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
      const buyPriceEl    = $("buyPrice");
      const wartAmountEl  = $("wartAmount");
      const sellPriceEl   = $("sellPrice");
      const tokenAmountEl = $("tokenAmount");
      const beforeTokenEl = $("beforeToken");
      const beforeWartEl  = $("beforeWart");
      const feePercentEl  = $("feePercent");
      const buyButton     = $("buyButton");
      const sellButton    = $("sellButton");
      const tbodyBuy      = $("tbodyBuy");
      const tbodySell     = $("tbodySell");
      const tbodyBuyers   = $("tbodyBuyers");
      const tbodySellers  = $("tbodySellers");

      // ── Field renderer (red border + tooltip) ──────────────────────
      function renderField(input, f) {
        input.classList.toggle("invalid", !f.valid);
        input.title = f.error || "";
      }

      // ── Row inserter (vanilla DOM, matches old behaviour) ──────────
      // `titles` is optional and holds a tooltip per cell. `deleteIndex`,
      // when given, appends the remove button carrying that row's index.
      function insertRow(obj, rowarr, id, titles, deleteIndex) {
        const row = obj.insertRow(-1);
        row.className = "p-4 h-9";
        for (let i = 0; i < rowarr.length; ++i) {
          const cell = row.insertCell(i);
          cell.className =
            "px-4 border-b border-blue-gray-50 font-sans text-sm antialiased font-normal leading-normal";
          if (i === rowarr.length - 1) cell.className += " " + id;
          cell.innerHTML = `${rowarr[i]}`;
          if (titles && titles[i]) cell.title = titles[i];
        }
        if (deleteIndex !== undefined) {
          const cell = row.insertCell(rowarr.length);
          cell.className =
            "px-4 border-b border-blue-gray-50 text-center w-10";
          const button = document.createElement("button");
          button.type = "button";
          button.textContent = "×";
          button.title = "Remove this order";
          button.dataset.deleteIndex = String(deleteIndex);
          button.className =
            "px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-gray-400 text-base leading-none hover:bg-gray-900 hover:text-white";
          cell.appendChild(button);
        }
      }

      // ── Single source of match() calls ─────────────────────────────
      // engine.match() always returns a full result; we re-render on
      // every change to keep the UI in sync.
      function tryMatch() {
        state.lastMatch = engine.match();
        renderOrderBooks();
        renderSummary();
        renderPool();
        drawArrows();
        scheduleUrlSync();
      }

      // The engine reports limits at full precision (they are exact
      // 16-bit-mantissa price-grid values, e.g. 1.732147216796875). The
      // order book columns are narrow, so the table shows a rounded
      // value and keeps the exact one in the tooltip.
      function fmtLimit(value) {
        const n = Number(value);
        if (!isFinite(n)) return String(value);
        let s = n.toPrecision(8);
        if (s.includes(".")) s = s.replace(/0+$/, "").replace(/\.$/, "");
        return s;
      }

      function renderOrderBooks() {
        const m = state.lastMatch;
        tbodyBuy.innerHTML = "";
        m.buys.forEach((o, i) => {
          insertRow(tbodyBuy, [fmtLimit(o.limit), o.amount, o.filled], "filledAmountWartItem", [o.limit], i);
        });
        tbodySell.innerHTML = "";
        m.sells.forEach((o, i) => {
          insertRow(tbodySell, [fmtLimit(o.limit), o.amount, o.filled], "filledAmountTokenItem", [o.limit], i);
        });
        let sumToken = 0;
        for (const el of document.getElementsByClassName("filledAmountTokenItem")) {
          sumToken += parseFloat(el.innerHTML);
        }
        let sumWart = 0;
        for (const el of document.getElementsByClassName("filledAmountWartItem")) {
          sumWart += parseFloat(el.innerHTML);
        }
        $("filledAmountToken").innerHTML = sumToken.toString();
        $("filledAmountWart").innerHTML  = sumWart.toString();
      }

      function renderSummary() {
        const m = state.lastMatch;
        tbodyBuyers.innerHTML = "";
        insertRow(tbodyBuyers, ["orders", m.matched.quote, m.matched.base, m.matched.price], "");
        if (m.toPool && m.toPool.isQuote) {
          insertRow(tbodyBuyers, ["via pool", m.toPool.quote, m.toPool.base, m.toPool.price], "");
        }
        insertRow(tbodyBuyers, ["total", m.filled.outQuoteBuyer, m.filled.inBaseBuyer, m.filled.priceBuyer], "");
        tbodySellers.innerHTML = "";
        insertRow(tbodySellers, ["orders", m.matched.base, m.matched.quote, m.matched.price], "");
        if (m.toPool && !m.toPool.isQuote) {
          insertRow(tbodySellers, ["via pool", m.toPool.base, m.toPool.quote, m.toPool.price], "");
        }
        insertRow(tbodySellers, ["total", m.filled.outBaseSeller, m.filled.inQuoteSeller, m.filled.priceSeller], "");
      }

      function renderPool() {
        const m = state.lastMatch;
        $("beforePrice").innerHTML = m.poolBefore.price;
        $("afterToken").innerHTML  = m.poolAfter.base;
        $("afterWart").innerHTML   = m.poolAfter.quote;
        $("afterPrice").innerHTML  = m.poolAfter.price;
      }

      // ── LeaderLine arrows ──────────────────────────────────────────
      const arrowTokenFromSeller = new LeaderLine($("sellTokenArrowPoint"), $("buyTokenArrowPoint"));
      const arrowTokenFromPool   = new LeaderLine($("poolInteractedTokenArrowPoint"), $("buyTokenArrowPoint"));
      const arrowWartFromBuyer   = new LeaderLine($("sellWartArrowPoint"), $("buyWartArrowPoint"), { color: "blue" });
      const arrowWartFromPool    = new LeaderLine($("poolInteractedWartArrowPoint"), $("buyWartArrowPoint"), { color: "blue" });
      const arrowWartToPool      = new LeaderLine($("sellWartArrowPoint"), $("poolInteractedWartArrowPoint"), { color: "blue" });
      const arrowTokenToPool     = new LeaderLine($("sellTokenArrowPoint"), $("poolInteractedTokenArrowPoint"));
      const allArrows = [
        arrowTokenFromSeller, arrowTokenFromPool,
        arrowWartFromBuyer,   arrowWartFromPool,
        arrowWartToPool,      arrowTokenToPool,
      ];
      for (const a of allArrows) a.hide();

      function drawArrows() {
        const m = state.lastMatch;
        for (const a of allArrows) { a.hide(); a.position(); }
        $("sellToken").innerHTML = m.filled.outBaseSeller;
        $("buyWart").innerHTML   = m.filled.inQuoteSeller;
        $("sellWart").innerHTML  = m.filled.outQuoteBuyer;
        $("buyToken").innerHTML  = m.filled.inBaseBuyer;
        if (m.toPool) {
          $("poolInteractedPrice").innerHTML = m.toPool.price;
          if (m.toPool.isQuote) {
            $("poolInteractedToken").innerHTML = "-" + m.toPool.base;
            $("poolInteractedWart").innerHTML  = "+" + m.toPool.quote;
          } else {
            $("poolInteractedToken").innerHTML = "+" + m.toPool.base;
            $("poolInteractedWart").innerHTML  = "-" + m.toPool.quote;
          }
        }
        if (m.matched && m.matched.base !== "0") {
          arrowTokenFromSeller.middleLabel = LeaderLine.pathLabel(m.matched.base);
          arrowTokenFromSeller.show();
        }
        if (m.matched && m.matched.quote !== "0") {
          arrowWartFromBuyer.middleLabel = LeaderLine.pathLabel(m.matched.quote);
          arrowWartFromBuyer.show();
        }
        if (m.toPool && m.toPool.isQuote) {
          arrowTokenFromPool.middleLabel = LeaderLine.pathLabel(m.toPool.base);
          arrowWartToPool.middleLabel    = LeaderLine.pathLabel(m.toPool.quote);
          arrowTokenFromPool.show();
          arrowWartToPool.show();
        }
        if (m.toPool && !m.toPool.isQuote) {
          arrowTokenToPool.middleLabel  = LeaderLine.pathLabel(m.toPool.base);
          arrowWartFromPool.middleLabel = LeaderLine.pathLabel(m.toPool.quote);
          arrowTokenToPool.show();
          arrowWartFromPool.show();
        }
      }

      // ── Button gating ──────────────────────────────────────────────
      function updateBuyButton() {
        buyButton.disabled = !(state.buyLimit.valid && state.buyAmount.valid);
      }
      function updateSellButton() {
        sellButton.disabled = !(state.sellLimit.valid && state.sellAmount.valid);
      }

      // ── Input handlers ─────────────────────────────────────────────
      // One place that pushes the two pool inputs into the engine and
      // updates their validity, so the typing path and the restore path
      // cannot drift apart.
      function applyPoolInputs() {
        const resBase = engine.setPool({ base: beforeTokenEl.value });
        state.poolBase.valid = "ok" in resBase;
        state.poolBase.error = "error" in resBase ? resBase.error : "";
        beforeTokenEl.style.backgroundColor = state.poolBase.valid ? "transparent" : "red";
        renderField(beforeTokenEl, state.poolBase);

        const resQuote = engine.setPool({ quote: beforeWartEl.value });
        state.poolQuote.valid = "ok" in resQuote;
        state.poolQuote.error = "error" in resQuote ? resQuote.error : "";
        beforeWartEl.style.backgroundColor = state.poolQuote.valid ? "transparent" : "red";
        renderField(beforeWartEl, state.poolQuote);

        tryMatch();
        updateBuyButton();
        updateSellButton();
      }

      beforeTokenEl.addEventListener("input", applyPoolInputs);
      beforeWartEl.addEventListener("input", applyPoolInputs);

      // ── Pool fee ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
      // The engine counts the fee in 1/10000 units, the input shows it
      // in percent. A percent that cannot be expressed in those units
      // (anything finer than 0.01) is rejected rather than rounded.
      function feeE4FromPercent(value) {
        const n = Number(value);
        if (!isFinite(n) || n < 0 || n > 99.99) return null;
        const scaled = n * 100;
        const rounded = Math.round(scaled);
        if (Math.abs(scaled - rounded) > 1e-9) return null;
        return rounded;
      }

      function percentFromFeeE4(feeE4) {
        return String(feeE4 / 100);
      }

      feePercentEl.addEventListener("input", () => {
        const feeE4 = feeE4FromPercent(feePercentEl.value);
        if (feeE4 === null) {
          // Leave the engine on its last valid fee; only the field is
          // marked so the user sees what needs fixing.
          state.fee.valid = false;
          state.fee.error = "The fee must be a percent in 0..99.99, in steps of 0.01";
        } else {
          const res = engine.setFeeE4(feeE4);
          state.fee.valid = "ok" in res;
          state.fee.error = "error" in res ? res.error : "";
          if (state.fee.valid) tryMatch();
        }
        feePercentEl.style.backgroundColor = state.fee.valid ? "transparent" : "red";
        renderField(feePercentEl, state.fee);
      });

      buyPriceEl.addEventListener("input", () => {
        const res = engine.validateLimit(buyPriceEl.value);
        state.buyLimit.valid = "ok" in res;
        state.buyLimit.error = "error" in res ? res.error : "";
        renderField(buyPriceEl, state.buyLimit);
        updateBuyButton();
      });
      wartAmountEl.addEventListener("input", () => {
        const res = engine.validateBaseAmount(wartAmountEl.value);
        state.buyAmount.valid = "ok" in res;
        state.buyAmount.error = "error" in res ? res.error : "";
        renderField(wartAmountEl, state.buyAmount);
        updateBuyButton();
      });
      sellPriceEl.addEventListener("input", () => {
        const res = engine.validateLimit(sellPriceEl.value);
        state.sellLimit.valid = "ok" in res;
        state.sellLimit.error = "error" in res ? res.error : "";
        renderField(sellPriceEl, state.sellLimit);
        updateSellButton();
      });
      tokenAmountEl.addEventListener("input", () => {
        const res = engine.validateQuoteAmount(tokenAmountEl.value);
        state.sellAmount.valid = "ok" in res;
        state.sellAmount.error = "error" in res ? res.error : "";
        renderField(tokenAmountEl, state.sellAmount);
        updateSellButton();
      });

      // Pool inputs: click parent to focus the inner input.
      $("parentBeforeToken").addEventListener("click", () => beforeTokenEl.focus());
      $("parentBeforeWart").addEventListener("click",  () => beforeWartEl.focus());

      // ── Button handlers ────────────────────────────────────────────
      buyButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const res = engine.addBuy({ limit: buyPriceEl.value, amount: wartAmountEl.value });
        if ("ok" in res) {
          tryMatch();
        } else {
          alert("Error: " + res.error);
        }
      });
      sellButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const res = engine.addSell({ limit: sellPriceEl.value, amount: tokenAmountEl.value });
        if ("ok" in res) {
          tryMatch();
        } else {
          alert("Error: " + res.error);
        }
      });

      // ── Delete order ───────────────────────────────────────────────
      // Delegated, because the rows are rebuilt on every match and
      // per-row listeners would be recreated with them. The index is the
      // row's position in the last match result, which is the order that
      // deleteBuyAt and deleteSellAt expect.
      tbodyBuy.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
        const button = e.target.closest("button[data-delete-index]");
        if (!button) return;
        if (engine.deleteBuyAt(Number(button.dataset.deleteIndex)) !== null) {
          tryMatch();
        }
      });
      tbodySell.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
        const button = e.target.closest("button[data-delete-index]");
        if (!button) return;
        if (engine.deleteSellAt(Number(button.dataset.deleteIndex)) !== null) {
          tryMatch();
        }
      });

      // ─── Initial state ────────────────────────────────────────────
      // The pool the page starts with, captured before a restore can
      // overwrite the inputs.
      const htmlPool = { base: beforeTokenEl.value, quote: beforeWartEl.value };

      // The engine reports the pool in its canonical 8-decimal form. Show
      // it the way a person would have typed it; the value parses back
      // to exactly the same integer either way.
      function trimDecimals(value) {
        return value.includes(".") ? value.replace(/0+$/, "").replace(/\.$/, "") : value;
      }

      // Adds one restored order from its exact price-grid bits.
      function addOrder(method, order) {
        const [limitBits, amount] = order;
        const res = engine[method]({ limitBits, amount });
        if (!("ok" in res)) {
          console.warn("Could not restore an order:", res.error);
        }
      }

      // A shared link restores the exact book and pool it was made from.
      // Without one, the demo starts from the HTML defaults (100 TOKEN,
      // 200 WART). The engine was already built with the restored
      // configuration above.
      if (restored) {
        beforeTokenEl.value = trimDecimals(restored.pool[0]);
        beforeWartEl.value = trimDecimals(restored.pool[1]);
        const res = engine.setPool({ base: restored.pool[0], quote: restored.pool[1] });
        if (!("ok" in res)) {
          console.warn("Could not restore the pool from ?state:", res.error);
        }
        for (const order of restored.buys ?? []) {
          addOrder("addBuy", order);
        }
        for (const order of restored.sells ?? []) {
          addOrder("addSell", order);
        }
        // The pool fields come straight from the engine, so they are
        // valid by construction.
        state.poolBase.valid = true;
        state.poolQuote.valid = true;
        state.poolBase.error = "";
        state.poolQuote.error = "";
        renderField(beforeTokenEl, state.poolBase);
        renderField(beforeWartEl, state.poolQuote);
      } else {
        // Push the HTML's default pool values (100 TOKEN, 200 WART) to
        // the engine so the initial render reflects the visible inputs.
        engine.setPool({ base: htmlPool.base, quote: htmlPool.quote });
      }

      // The fee field always mirrors the engine: on a restored link the
      // engine was built with the payload's fee, otherwise it has the
      // demo default. Writing it from getConfig keeps both in sync.
      feePercentEl.value = percentFromFeeE4(engine.getConfig().feeE4);
      state.fee.valid = true;
      state.fee.error = "";
      feePercentEl.style.backgroundColor = "transparent";
      renderField(feePercentEl, state.fee);

      // Validate buy/sell fields with empty defaults (they stay invalid
      // until the user types). Arrow functions preserve the `engine`
      // binding — Embind exposes methods bound to the instance only at
      // the method-call site, not when stored in a variable.
      for (const [el, key, validator] of [
        [buyPriceEl,    "buyLimit",   (v) => engine.validateLimit(v)],
        [wartAmountEl,  "buyAmount",  (v) => engine.validateBaseAmount(v)],
        [sellPriceEl,   "sellLimit",  (v) => engine.validateLimit(v)],
        [tokenAmountEl, "sellAmount", (v) => engine.validateQuoteAmount(v)],
      ]) {
        if (el.value) {
          const res = validator(el.value);
          state[key].valid = "ok" in res;
          state[key].error = "error" in res ? res.error : "";
          renderField(el, state[key]);
        }
      }
      updateBuyButton();
      updateSellButton();

      // The default demo state (no orders, the pool the page starts
      // with) is what an untouched page shows, so the URL stays clean
      // until the user changes something.
      {
        const scratch = new FbmEngine({ baseDecimals: 8, feeE4: 5 });
        scratch.setPool({ base: htmlPool.base, quote: htmlPool.quote });
        defaultState = encodeMatch(scratch.match(), scratch.getConfig());
      }
      tryMatch();

      // ── Copy shareable link ───────────────────────────────────────
      const copyStatus = $("copyLinkStatus");
      let copyStatusTimer = null;
      function showCopyStatus(text) {
        copyStatus.textContent = text;
        if (copyStatusTimer) clearTimeout(copyStatusTimer);
        copyStatusTimer = setTimeout(() => {
          copyStatusTimer = null;
          copyStatus.textContent = "";
        }, 2500);
      }
      $("copyLinkButton").addEventListener("click", async () => {
        // Make sure the address bar holds the current state before
        // copying it.
        try {
          const url = new URL(window.location.href);
          const encoded = encodeState();
          if (encoded && encoded !== defaultState) url.searchParams.set(STATE_PARAM, encoded);
          else url.searchParams.delete(STATE_PARAM);
          history.replaceState(null, "", url.toString());
        } catch (err) {
          console.warn("Could not update the URL:", err);
        }
        const link = window.location.href;
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(link);
          showCopyStatus("Link copied");
        } catch {
          // Clipboard access needs a secure context; fall back to a
          // selectable field so the link can still be copied by hand.
          if (copyStatusTimer) {
            clearTimeout(copyStatusTimer);
            copyStatusTimer = null;
          }
          const field = document.createElement("input");
          field.value = link;
          field.readOnly = true;
          field.className =
            "w-96 rounded-md border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1 text-sm";
          // Note: the field is a child of the status element, so the
          // status text is appended rather than assigned.
          copyStatus.replaceChildren("Copy the selected link: ", field);
          field.focus();
          field.select();
        }
      });
    </script>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
